        "sim": {
          "kind": "subckt",
          "element": "",
          "name": "IP2332",
          "text": ".subckt IP2332 ntc iset led2 led1 bat lx gnd vin\n* IP2332 behavioural model (averaged synchronous buck charger, one Li-ion cell, 4.2 V).\n* The switching is replaced by a voltage source on LX; control signals are in amps (1 V = 1 A).\nVone one gnd DC 1\nV43 v43 gnd DC 4.3\nV6 v6 gnd DC 6\nV03 v03 gnd DC 0.3\nV049 v049 gnd DC 0.49\nV18 v18 gnd DC 1.8\nV273 v273 gnd DC 2.73\nV3 v3 gnd DC 3.0\nV415 v415 gnd DC 4.15\nV42 v42 gnd DC 4.2\nV41 v41 gnd DC 4.1\nV2a v2a gnd DC 2.0\nV8m v8m gnd DC 0.00833\nVcl vcl gnd DC 3.3\n* ISET: a 1 V reference through 1 ohm; the current in RISET sets the charge current, ICC = 0.35 + 2.75 / RISET[kohm],\n* 2 A when ISET is open (RISET >= 120k). x = current in mA.\nSref v1 ref vin v43 SWC\nVr1 v1 gnd DC 1\nRref ref gnd 100Meg\nRm ref iset 1\nEx x gnd ref iset 1000\nVo35 ci0 gnd DC 0.35\nEcc ci1 ci0 x gnd 2.75\nSa ci1 icc x v8m SWC\nSb v2a icc v8m x SWC\nRicc icc gnd 100k\n* NTC: 100 uA into the pin; the voltage tells the temperature (0.3-0.49 V warm, 0.49-1.8 V normal, 1.8-2.73 V cool)\nIntc gnd ntc 100u\nDcl ntc vcl DCL\nRntc ntc gnd 100Meg\nEhalf ichalf gnd icc gnd 0.5\nSh1 icc ie v18 ntc SWC\nSh2 ichalf ie ntc v18 SWC\nRie ie gnd 100k\nSv1 v42 vcvn ntc v049 SWC\nSv2 v41 vcvn v049 ntc SWC\nRvcv vcvn gnd 100k\n* the charger runs for 4.3 V < VIN < 6 V and a cell temperature that is not too hot or too cold\nSg1 one n1 vin v43 SWC\nSg2 n1 n2 v6 vin SWC\nSg3 n2 n3 ntc v03 SWC\nSg4 n3 on v273 ntc SWC\nRon on gnd 1k\nRn1 n1 gnd 100Meg\nRn2 n2 gnd 100Meg\nRn3 n3 gnd 100Meg\n* pre-charge (below 3 V) is a fifth of ICC; above it the current is the smaller of the limit and the voltage loop\nEk ik gnd ie gnd 0.2\nSk1 ie ia bat v3 SWC\nSk2 ik ia v3 bat SWC\nRia ia gnd 100k\nEb cb gnd vcvn bat 60\nSma ia m cb ia SWC\nSmb cb m ia cb SWC\nRm m gnd 100k\nSu m u on gnd SWG\nRu u gnd 100k\n* output stage: LX = cell voltage + 3 V/A x (reference - current) + an integral term, limited to 0 .. VIN, and never pushing back into VIN\nEcm cm gnd u s 3\nGint gnd cint u s 0.02\nCint cint gnd 1u\nRint cint gnd 10k\nEd0 d0 cm bat gnd 1\nEd d d0 cint gnd 1\nSc1 d c1 vin d SWC\nSc2 vin c1 d vin SWC\nRc1 c1 gnd 100k\nSc3 c1 c2 c1 gnd SWC\nSc4 gnd c2 gnd c1 SWC\nRc2 c2 gnd 100k\nElx ls gnd c2 gnd 1\nRsn ls ls2 0.001\nEs s gnd ls ls2 1000\nSd ls2 lx ls2 lx SWD\nRlx lx gnd 100Meg\n* the input current is taken equal to the output current (a real buck draws less)\nGin vin gnd ls ls2 1000\nRiq vin gnd 1k\n* LED1 (5 mA constant current) while charging, LED2 while full; both off at a fault (no blinking is modelled)\nEik10 icc10 gnd ie gnd 0.1\nSchg1 on chg s icc10 SWC\nSchg2 on chg v415 bat SWC\nRchg chg gnd 1k\nSfl1 on fa icc10 s SWC\nSfl2 fa fl bat v415 SWC\nRfa fa gnd 100Meg\nRfl fl gnd 1k\nGl1 vin led1 chg gnd 0.005\nDl1 led1 vin DCL\nRl1 led1 gnd 100Meg\nSl2 vin led2 fl gnd SWL\nRl2 led2 gnd 100Meg\n.model SWC SW(RON=1 ROFF=1G VT=0 VW=0.001)\n.model SWG SW(RON=1 ROFF=1G VT=0.5 VW=0.1)\n.model SWD SW(RON=0.17 ROFF=1G VT=0 VW=0.002)\n.model SWL SW(RON=100 ROFF=1G VT=0.5 VW=0.1)\n.model DCL D(IS=1e-12 N=1)\n.ends IP2332",
          "pins": [
            "1",
            "2",
            "3",
            "4",
            "5",
            "6",
            "7",
            "8"
          ],
          "params": {
            "icc_open": 2.0,
            "vfloat": 4.2
          }
        }
      }
    },
